From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:10:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 364/366] dt-bindings: input: gpio-matrix-keypad: add
 needs-ghost-filter

A key matrix without a diode per key ghosts. When three pressed keys sit
on three corners of a rectangle, the fourth corner also reads as
pressed. The scan cannot tell that phantom from a real fourth key.

Add a boolean that marks such a matrix, so the driver can ignore
ambiguous scans. The name and meaning follow google,needs-ghost-filter
in the cros-ec-keyb binding.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml     | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
index 7a0de5648..a9fab526b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
@@ -82,6 +82,14 @@ properties:
       Drive inactive columns during scan,
       default is to turn inactive columns into inputs.
 
+  needs-ghost-filter:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The matrix has no diode per key, so three pressed keys on the corners
+      of a rectangle make the fourth corner read as pressed. Ignore any scan
+      in which two columns share more than one pressed key, until the
+      ambiguity clears.
+
   wakeup-source: true
 
 required:
